Pooled blocks of 16 MiB at most instead of 64 MiB: on a guest whose device memory is wired guest RAM a pool's
blocks double up to the cap and stay wired whole (NativeMetal 45c8294's bridge patch 0021, lost at the move to 555b13d).

diff --git a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs
index 688a99612..872c7e371 100644
--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/memory.rs
@@ -198,10 +198,15 @@ use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
 pub(crate) mod making_parts;
 mod ready;
 
-/// The size of a pooled block of a heap of 1 GiB or more, at most the device's
+/// The size of a pooled block of a heap of 256 MiB or more, at most the device's
 /// `maxMemoryAllocationSize`: the largest pooled block ([`pooled_block_bytes`]); a heap whose
-/// blocks are smaller is small ([`Memory::small`]).
-pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 64 << 20;
+/// blocks are smaller is small ([`Memory::small`]). 16 MiB: where device memory is the system's
+/// own and wired as a block is made (a guest whose GPU imports its pages), a pool's blocks double
+/// up to this ([`FIRST_BLOCK_BYTES`]) and a partly filled or kept empty one of 64 MiB stays wired
+/// whole: a macOS guest's WindowServer held 623 MiB in blocks of up to 80 MiB and its icon agent
+/// 267 MiB (two blocks of 64 MiB and one of 68) where a new one that drew the same icons held
+/// 121 MiB in blocks of 4 to 24 MiB (2026-11-16).
+pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 16 << 20;
 
 /// The most of its heap a pooled block takes: a sixteenth ([`pooled_block_bytes`]).
 const BLOCK_HEAP_SHARE: u64 = 16;
